Z||000012||cadaver||08-15-2001||12:35 AM||||Just remove the tail lights open them up and pull the red lenses out.||||reg||1
Z||000013||qwikgta||08-15-2001||01:00 PM||||It really is that easy, just remove the whole taillight asmbly and be very careful when you "seperate" the two halfs.  It is glued with a black type of silicon or something.  Then remove the lens, I painted mine because alot of the chrome was missing and try diff ideas, like painting the center "unused" part body color or black.  I am going to redo mine and paint parts red/black.  THen go out and get red lens.  I got mine at PEPBOYS, they are not the same ones that "we" use, the part number was 1157 or something like that, but they fit, just takes some time so you dont brake them.<P>I will try to write some things up<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000014||85ZainoGT||08-15-2001||01:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B>qwikgta, luv the stuff.  Just might do the clear tails thing.  Now could you guys write some emails deatiling how you did the stuff and send them to gregman_1@excite.com ?  I'm working on the homemade mods database so Cliff will have something to link to from the opening page.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>id like some details too on how to do those things   automaticj5@aol.com thanks if you do send... and another thing, would it look bad if I took random things off the interior of my car and painted them silver(as accents) like the gauge cover, door handles and stuff like that?  and is there anywhere where I can buy a new shift knob? thanks...||||reg||1
Z||000015||Steven||08-15-2001||01:45 PM||||First off I have to say that I don't have a parking brake. None. The rear calipers where replaced with frt. calipers and new rear rotors turn to the thickness of new frt rotors replaced the old rear ones. This not the mod that I want to tell everyone about, but it is the needed background info that tells why I have a park brake lever in the car that controls nothing....until now.<P>One day about a couple of weeks ago, I was stuck in some rush hour construction on US-23. Now I knew that I was goint to be stuck there for a while. The only thing to do was try and find a good radio station, watch the temp gauge go up and wait to hear the cooling fan come on. Now my car does not have a/c, so there is no way to force the fan on early. I start think about putting an over ride switch in, but I would want a light of something to remind me that I had turned the fan on. That is where the park brake lever came in to play. With this in mind I pulled the service manual out when I got home and did some checking on the wiring. Turns out that the bulk head connector that goes thur the frt fire wall has a green w/black strip wire that is the ground wire for the cooling fan relay. With two splicing connectors, and about two feet of wire I spliced that wire to the purple wire that goes to the park brake lever switch. Now when ever the park brake lever is pulled. It turns on the cooling fan. Total cost: less than two bucks.<P><BR>Sorry I guess I was long winded.||||reg||1
Z||000016||b lo 0||08-15-2001||04:49 PM||||QwickGTA, I did the clear tails thing last night as soon as I got off the net.  Looks really cool!  I left mine with the black panel in the middle.  Goin up to Manny, Moe and Jacks today for some red bulbs.  It's SOOO easy, this is exactly the kind of stuff I was looking for.  Just pull up the prongs, peel off the cover, remove color peices, and put it back together.  The GT has smoke-lookin taillight lenses, so it looks even cooler.  Great idea!||||reg||1
Z||000017||MD_Fiero||08-15-2001||11:13 PM|||| i did it too...really cool..tho i only did my reverse so far...doing some custom lights...but not tellin how their going to be done untill im done<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||b lo 0||08-15-2001||11:55 PM||||Alright, now I have one of my own.  A few months ago, I got a totaled '83 Honda Accord for free.  I'm using the hood vents from this car on the Fiero, and tonight, I took the lighter, with the cool lighted green trim ring, and put it in the GT.  Looks really cool at night, and looks a little better than the stock lighter during the day.  Also reuses the same element, as the cup is the same depth as the stock lighter.  The guys who go to the ATL cruise-in Saturday will be able to see the clear tails as well as the lighter.  A few more things are coming off the Honda and into the Fiero, such as the LED-style in-dash gear indicator (gonna be helpful when I put in the ratchet shifter) and a vehicle info center.  Keep ya updated...||||reg||1
Z||000019||MD_Fiero||08-16-2001||11:07 AM||||sounds nice...get pic's <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||San Fran||09-19-2001||11:38 PM||||Going to change the look of my '86 2m4 (with V6)  Soon to be 200+ horses as well.  <P>This is going to cost minimal, just a lot of hours during the winter.<P>Going to change the front, rear fascias, put rocker panels on and a custom spoiler.  Going to lower the car by 2" as well.<P>The front spoiler is going to be lowered (following the Fieros lines) so that the pointy look is gone.  The rocker panels are going to get smaller in the middle and larger at the wheels, like the BMW's.  The rear fascia is going to have a lowered look with cutouts for the two dual tips I have, showing about an inch of the stainless steel on both sides.  Going to add to the notchback where it attaches to the trunk as well, to give it a better, more rounded (aerodynamic)look?  <P>The spoiler may be off the 2003 Dodge Viper prototype (have the mold and customized will to fit the Fiero) or we'll make our own custom spoiler.<P>With the new smoking red paint job (It'll be like a mirror so those with mullets will be able to use it to comb their hair), Fiero owners are going to drool (well at least the same ones).<P>We're going to follow the lines on the Fiero so it is going to look sweet.  May also get rid of the lights (try and get the 300ZX look) and side mirrors.<P>I'll post before and after photos in the spring when It'll be done.<P>------------------<BR>[img]http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1626330&a=12427866&p=45623747 [/img]<P>'86 2m4 modified w/2.8||||reg||1
Z||000021||San Fran||09-19-2001||11:39 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1626330&a=12427866&p=45623747"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>[img]http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1626330&a=12427866&p=45623747 [/img]<P>'86 2m4 modified w/2.8||||reg||1
Z||000022||Captain Fireball||09-20-2001||12:02 AM||||Ok, how's this? I have an 86 fiero, 4 cylinder. Ugly grey (going to get a paint job soon. Probably black with a nice high gloss) but aside from that everything's stock. Anyone able to quote me on a price (please list if canadian or american dollars canadian preferred) to upgrade to either a v6 2.8L or even just another engine or kit to up performance and maybe even toss in some pricing for any exterior work you think might be a good idea. I like the inexpensive ideas, and unfortunately money is a bit of an object, but I would like to know mostly about an engine upgrade. K&N filters and mufflers might be the first on.||||reg||10
Z||000023||falconhulk||09-20-2001||10:24 AM||||Why would you want to remove the decklid grills?  ||||reg||1
Z||000024||StuGood||09-20-2001||07:01 PM||||This is so simple, you can hardly to call it a "mod."  But it was almost no-cost, and it pleased me greatly, so <B>there</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Walking along one day, happened to find a 1/4" wing nut (might have been 5/16, but whatever), so picked it up and put in my pocket.  Had no real plans for it. Carried it in my jacket pocket for many moons; never much thought about it.<P>Never cared for the fact that somewhere along the way, air cleaners quit having wing nuts on top - nowadays they just have plain nuts.  Somehow I just expect to see a wing nut there.<P>On a whim, while working on my car, I ran a metric tap through that wing nut I had found, and it took the metric threads beautifully!  Didn't even have to tap-drill it.  Painted to to match the color scheme of my air cleaner, screwed it on, and now I'm a contented camper    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>   ||||reg||10
